e\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Fire%20Axe\"><img alt=\"Fire Axe\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Fire_Axe_33d4f5.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot3\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Terra%20Legs\"><img alt=\"Terra Legs\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Terra_Legs_43b41b.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot4\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Tower%20Shield\"><img alt=\"Tower Shield\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Tower_Shield_ea3208.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot5\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Sapphire Hammer\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Sapphire_Hammer_7196f7.gif\" width=\"32\"/></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">9.80<br/>December 12, 2012<br/>Winter Update 2012</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p>The <b>Caves of the Lost</b> can be found deep under the <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarf%20Mines\">mines of Kazordoon</a>. <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarves\">The Lost</a> are renegade dwarves that have been driven to insanity in the dark mines.\nThere are five caves in total. One cave is accessible from Kazordoon (main entrance <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32625,31852,14\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32625, 31852, 14)</a>). This cave ends up with an upper level of Dwarves Guards leading to another lower level with 3 seperate small caves of Losts. Other three caves are accessible from regular Dwarf Mines (<a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32477,31974,14\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32477, 31974, 14)</a>, <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32465,31940,14\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32465, 31940, 14)</a>, and <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32424,31853,14\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32424, 31853, 14)</a>). The fifth cave is found in <a href=\"#/wiki/Mount%20Sternum%2FUndead%20Cave\">Mount Sternum</a>, <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32463,31986,14\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32463, 31986, 14)</a>.\n</p><p>It is a good hunting place for paladins or mages, but not as good for knights. Throwers and Hushers will always keep a distance, so chasing them would result in luring more losts, which can end up for us badly. Furthermore, Bashers and Enslaved Dwarves are very heavily melee fighters, so we will use a lot of potions fighting them. Although there is a trick for knights trying to hunt the distance ones (lure them against the wall, and throw energy walls on the sides, so they have no path to escape), but melee ones will still do you a lot of harm.\n</p><p><a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarven%20Ring\">Dwarven Ring</a> is a must-have while hunting here. All 4 monsters cause heavy drunkenness. Also remember to bring a lot of energy walls. Any AoE runes would also come in handy, as Throwers and Hushers goes invisible very often. As Free Account player you choose Avalanche Runes. As Premium Account player you definitely want Thunderstorm Runes. If you know where the invisible enemy is standing, you should use cheaper Explosion Rune just to reveal them.\n</p><p>Their weakest element is Holy (damage taken around 100% - 110%), so Paladins will have a nice time here. Other elements that are worth mentioning are Physical (90% - 103%) and Energy (90% - 95%). Death and Ice are slightly lower (around 80% - 90%). Fire and Earth are the worst elements here, because three Lost Dwarves are totally immune to Earth, while Enslaved Dwarf is immune to Fire.\n</p><p>Both <a href=\"#/wiki/Malech\">Malech</a> and the <a href=\"#/wiki/Shortsighted%20Dwarf\">Shortsighted Dwarf</a> can tell more about <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarves\">The Lost</a>.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Creatures\">Creatures</span></h2>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Lost%20Thrower\"><img alt=\"Lost Thrower\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Lost_Thrower_3a0987.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></span><br/><a href=\"#/wiki/Lost%20Thrower\">Lost Thrower</a></td><td style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">1,500</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">1,700</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">700+</td><td style=\"font-size: small;\"><div class=\"loot-table\" id=\"w-loot_perc_loot\">\n<ul><li>1-14